      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: dangerous driving behaviors: alcohol and drugs, implied consent, distracted and drowsy driving",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: dangerous driving behaviors: alcohol and drugs, implied consent, distracted and drowsy driving\nAudience: every first-time Wisconsin Class D applicant, and above all permit and probationary drivers, who face the zero alcohol limit and the emergency-only phone rule.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: the chapter sets the alcohol, drug, implied consent and phone rules [A01] and the distraction habits and drowsy driving warning signs [A02].\nLevel: rule recall with legal consequences; light load but high stakes.\nPrerequisites: the license progression section on instruction permits and probationary licenses.\n",
